{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2589","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2589","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2589\",\"parent_revision\":\"7273f07544239266d2ed046a20e13be7c02cc5ec65182962fcbd78d172ca1b63\",\"root_revision\":\"7273f07544239266d2ed046a20e13be7c02cc5ec65182962fcbd78d172ca1b63\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-06-15\\n-->\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- Test is non-deterministic: passes when rate limit is not active, fails when it is\\n- Masks whether the \\\"skip edit when unchanged\\\" logic actually works\\n- Contributes to secondary rate limit exhaustion during CI runs that exercise many GitHub-API-touching tests in sequence\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **fix: test_set_manifest_skips_edit_when_body_unchanged hits live github api \u2014 should be fully mocked** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: cast() removal session 2026-06-05\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-06-05\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-06-08)\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-08T08:14:03.294627Z</sub>\\n\\n- Goal: Fix `test_set_manifest_skips_edit_when_body_unchanged` so it never hits the live GitHub API and correctly exercises the intended no-op path in `set_manifest`.\\\\n- Status: APPROVED-WITH-GAPS\\\\n- AVAILABLE:\\\\n  - The failing test file and implementation are present and readable\\\\n  - The mock fixture gap is directly observable: `mock_repo` patches `get_github` but not `_make_github_client`\\\\n  - The working test `test_set_manifest_calls_issue_edit_when_body_changes` shows the correct mock pattern\\\\n- DERIVABLE:\\\\n  - The exact mock gap: `_get_gist` calls `_make_github_client()` directly, bypassing the `get_github` mock\\\\n  - The behavior mismatch: `set_manifest` has no equality check; the no-op optimization in the test name does not exist in the implementation\\\\n- MISSING:\\\\n  - Decision: add the no-op optimization to `set_manifest` (fix implementation to match test intent) OR rename and rewrite the test to match current behavior\\n</div>\\n\\n### Artifact Classification\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-08T08:14:19.104471Z</sub>\\n\\n- Primary artifact type: Bug fix (test defect + possible implementation gap)\\\\n- Behavioral boundary: `set_manifest` must never call the live GitHub API in unit tests; `test_set_manifest_skips_edit_when_body_unchanged` must assert `gist.edit` is NOT called when content is unchanged\\\\n- Domain-semantic evaluation target: Acceptance criteria must prove that `gist.edit` is never called under unchanged-content conditions, with no live network calls, by running the test with `GITHUB_TOKEN` unset\\n</div>\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-08T08:14:37.849457Z</sub>\\n\\n1. Ensure `GITHUB_TOKEN` is set (a real token with gist scope) and GitHub secondary rate limits are active\\\\n2. Run: `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/tests_backlog/test_artifact_provider.py::TestGitHubArtifactProviderSetManifest::test_set_manifest_skips_edit_when_body_unchanged -v`\\\\n3. Observe: test fails with `403 RateLimitExceededException` when rate limits are active; when limits are inactive the test may appear to pass but is making real API calls\\\\n4. Alternative: set `GITHUB_TOKEN=\\\"\\\"` and run \u2014 the test fails because `_make_github_client` is not mocked and tries to authenticate with an empty token\\n</div>\\n\\n### Output / Evidence\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-08T08:15:12.959990Z</sub>\\n\\n- `mock_repo` fixture (line 61 of `test_artifact_provider.py`) patches `backlog_core.artifact_provider.get_github` but does NOT patch `backlog_core.artifact_provider._make_github_client`\\\\n- `_get_gist` (line 694 of `artifact_provider.py`) calls `_make_github_client()` directly \u2014 not `get_github()` \u2014 so the mock chain breaks there; any code path that calls `_get_gist` with a body containing the gist sentinel reaches the live API\\\\n- `set_manifest` (lines 531-533 of `artifact_provider.py`) calls `_get_gist` then `gist.edit()` unconditionally; there is no equality check or no-op path\\\\n- The test's own inline comment (lines 496-497) states: \\\"body WILL differ from updated_body \u2192 mutation IS called again\\\" \u2014 directly contradicting the test name `skips_edit_when_body_unchanged`\\\\n- The working test `test_set_manifest_calls_issue_edit_when_body_changes` (line 411) shows the correct pattern: it patches `_make_github_client` via `mocker.patch(\\\"backlog_core.artifact_provider._make_github_client\\\")` as a local step inside the test body\\n</div>\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-08T08:15:54.064390Z</sub>\\n\\n7/10 \u2014 CI non-determinism. The test makes live GitHub API calls during CI runs, contributing to secondary rate limit exhaustion that can cascade and fail other tests. Not a data-loss or security risk, but directly undermines test suite reliability and masks whether the no-op optimization exists.\\n</div>\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-08T08:16:34.645932Z</sub>\\n\\n- Blocks: Test suite reliability \u2014 tests that should be fully mocked make real API calls non-deterministically\\\\n- Bottleneck: CI stability; secondary rate limit exhaustion from this test cascades to other GitHub-touching tests in the same run\\\\n- Masks: Whether a no-op optimization (skip `gist.edit` when content unchanged) actually works \u2014 it does not exist in the current implementation\\n</div>\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-08T08:17:30.390017Z</sub>\\n\\n- Test suite no longer hits the live GitHub API for this case; passes reliably with `GITHUB_TOKEN` unset\\\\n- If the no-op optimization is also added to `set_manifest`: reduces unnecessary `gist.edit()` calls in production, lowering secondary rate limit consumption\\\\n- Establishes the correct pattern for mocking `_make_github_client` independently of `get_github` in future tests for `_get_gist`-touching code paths\\n</div>\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-08T08:18:25.538620Z</sub>\\n\\nWhen `set_manifest` is called with logically identical content, the second call should not invoke `gist.edit()`. The complete mock chain must be established: both `get_github` (for GraphQL operations in `_fetch_issue_graphql` and `_update_issue_graphql`) and `_make_github_client` (for Gist object fetch inside `_get_gist`) must be patched so no live network calls are made. The test must assert `mock_gist.edit.assert_not_called()` after the no-change invocation. Running this test with `GITHUB_TOKEN` unset or invalid must not cause a network error.\\n</div>\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-08T08:19:52.889944Z</sub>\\n\\nAfter the fix:\\\\n- `uv run pytest ...::test_set_manifest_skips_edit_when_body_unchanged` passes when `GITHUB_TOKEN` is unset\\\\n- The test contains `mocker.patch(\\\"backlog_core.artifact_provider._make_github_client\\\")` returning a mock gist\\\\n- The test body contains `mock_gist.edit.assert_not_called()` after the second `set_manifest` call\\\\n- Either `set_manifest` contains an equality check comparing serialized manifest content before calling `gist.edit()`, OR the test is renamed to reflect the actual behavior and a placeholder test describes the not-yet-implemented optimization\\\\n- The no-op path (if implemented) uses a stable content comparison that is not affected by timestamp differences on repeated calls with the same logical manifest content\\n</div>\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-08T08:26:43.400338Z</sub>\\n\\n1. Test passes with `GITHUB_TOKEN` unset \u2014 zero live API dependency.\\\\n2. Test asserts `mock_gist.edit.assert_not_called()` after second `set_manifest` call with unchanged content.\\\\n3. `backlog_core.artifact_provider._make_github_client` is patched so `_get_gist` uses mock gist, not live PyGithub client.\\\\n4. If no-op optimization added to `set_manifest`: equality check is timestamp-stable; first new-content call invokes `gist.edit()`, second identical call does not.\\\\n5. If test is renamed instead: new name describes actual behavior exercised; separate test documents the not-yet-implemented optimization.\\\\n6. Full `TestGitHubArtifactProviderSetManifest` class passes with zero live network calls.\\n</div>\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-08T08:24:43.373606Z</sub>\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\\\n|------|------|\\\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/artifact_provider.py` \u2014 `GitHubGistArtifactProvider.set_manifest` (lines 504-539) |\\\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/artifact_provider.py` \u2014 `GitHubGistArtifactProvider._get_gist` (lines 680-698) |\\\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/tests_backlog/test_artifact_provider.py` \u2014 `TestGitHubArtifactProviderSetManifest` class |\\\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/tests_backlog/test_artifact_provider.py` \u2014 `mock_repo` fixture (line 61) \u2014 patches `get_github` only |\\\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/tests_backlog/test_artifact_provider.py` \u2014 `test_set_manifest_calls_issue_edit_when_body_changes` (line 392) \u2014 correct mock pattern reference |\\n</div>\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-08T08:13:35.829760Z</sub>\\n\\n- Depends on: None \u2014 self-contained test fix\\n- Blocks: Test suite reliability in CI; unblocks confidently running the full test suite without requiring a live GitHub token\\n</div>\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-08T08:13:39.473973Z</sub>\\n\\n- Decision needed: add the no-op optimization to `set_manifest` (fix the implementation to match the test name) OR rename and rewrite the test to match current implementation behavior. Either path is valid but the choice affects scope.\\n</div>\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-08T08:25:35.917505Z</sub>\\n\\nSmall-to-Medium depending on scope decision. Test-only fix (patch `_make_github_client`, fix assertion, rename test): Small \u2014 one file, root cause directly observable. Adding the no-op optimization to `set_manifest` plus test rewrite: Medium \u2014 two files, requires a stable equality check that is not affected by the `last_updated` timestamp stamped inside `set_manifest`.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`tests_backlog/test_artifact_provider.py::TestGitHubArtifactProviderSetManifest::test_set_manifest_skips_edit_when_body_unchanged` makes a live call to `gist.edit()` against the real GitHub API. The mock chain breaks before reaching the edit call, so the test hits real GitHub and triggers a 403 RateLimitExceededException when GitHub secondary rate limits are active.\\n\\nThe test name says \\\"skips_edit_when_body_unchanged\\\" but the body IS being changed in the test, causing `set_manifest` to reach the `gist.edit()` call path and hit the live API.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Root Cause\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThe mock for the gist object doesn't properly simulate the `gist.raw_data` comparison that determines whether the body changed. The equality check passes unexpectedly, the edit path is taken, and the real GitHub API is called.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nEnsure the mock's `gist.raw_data` (or `gist.files[\\\"manifest.json\\\"].content`) returns the same value as the manifest being set, so the equality check correctly triggers the \\\"no change\\\" path and `gist.edit()` is never called. Assert that `gist.edit` was NOT called after `provider.set_manifest(...)`.\\n</div>\\n\\n## File\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`plugins/development-harness/tests_backlog/test_artifact_provider.py` \u2014 `TestGitHubArtifactProviderSetManifest` class\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"770469b4a939f60e6e0de6d2ad6e8aa1b30648449b7b9ad04917fc1a279de667\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCLOPA\"}"}